Sleep = 500 ms

Work = 2 seconds

Still fine.

The workflow becomes:

Thread sleeps 0.5 seconds

Thread wakes up

Thread continues remaining 1.5 seconds of work

Thread completes normally

There is no requirement that sleep time must match work time.

🟥 VERY IMPORTANT MISCONCEPTION TO FIX
❌ Sleep does not guarantee that thread finishes work
❌ Sleep does not guarantee that thread gives up lock
❌ Sleep does not kill or stop a thread
✔ Sleep only pauses the thread temporarily
✔ After sleep, thread continues normally
✔ And if thread was holding a lock, it STILL holds it
